        <ol class="c13 lst-kix_list_10-0" start="3">
            <li class="c1 c6 li-bullet-0"><span class="c2">We are an independent rating agency and may determine, apply and amend our methodologies and any Rating in our sole discretion from time to time.</span></li>
        </ol>
        <p class="c1 c4 c15"><span class="c2"></span></p>
        <ol class="c13 lst-kix_list_7-0" start="4">
            <li class="c1 c6 li-bullet-0"><span class="c19 c5 c3">Acceptance/non-acceptance and use of Rating</span></li>
        </ol>
        <p class="c1 c4"><span class="c19 c5 c3"></span></p>
        <ol class="c13 lst-kix_list_9-0 start" start="1">
            <li class="c1 c6 li-bullet-0"><span class="c3">After ICRA has informed your Company of the Rating it has assigned, your Company shall communicate its decision to ICRA regarding its acceptance of the Rating in writing, and intended use of the Rating, in any manner, within 5 (five) working days of the assignment of the Rating. In the event your Company fails to notify ICRA of its decision regarding its acceptance/non-acceptance of the Rating or failed to appeal against the Rating during such 5 (five) working days acceptance time period, such failure shall be treated by ICRA as non-acceptance of the Rating and the Rating shall be disclosed by ICRA on its website, within 30 (thirty) days of communication of Rating by ICRA, as unaccepted Rating. Any use by you of the Rating shall be deemed acceptance of the Rating. Also, in case any rating of the Security is published or otherwise disseminated by any other rating agency at any stage, or any other circumstances that ICRA may deem fit, ICRA will reserve the right to publish the Rating within a reasonable period of time.</span></li>
        </ol>
        <p class="c1 c4 c15"><span class="c2"></span></p>
        <ol class="c13 lst-kix_list_9-0" start="2">
            <li class="c1 c6 li-bullet-0" id="h.1fob9te"><span class="c2">During such 5 (five) working days as mentioned in Clause D (I), the Rating shall remain confidential subject to the terms of this Agreement, including without limitation, clause N (Applicant Confidentiality for Unpublished ratings). On request, an unaccepted Rating may be converted to an accepted Rating, provided such request is made by your Company within 2 (two) months from the date ICRA first communicated its Rating decision to you. However, before such conversion is made, the Rating initially assigned may have to undergo a revalidation process. No additional fee would be charged to your Company for the conversion, unless the Rating initially assigned needs to undergo a revalidation process. The Rating initially assigned needs to undergo a revalidation process if either (i) the size of the Security or structure of the Security has changed before the Rating has been accepted by your Company, provided the revised size should not exceed the Security (which would constitute an enhancement not covered by or under this Agreement), or (ii) the request for conversion is received by ICRA after 2 (two) months from the date that ICRA first communicated its Rating decision to you. </span></li>
        </ol>
        <p class="c1 c4 c15"><span class="c2"></span></p>
        <ol class="c13 lst-kix_list_9-0" start="3">
            <li class="c1 c6 li-bullet-0"><span class="c2">In case a Rating is not accepted by your Company, or in case of failure of your Company to notify its acceptance or non-acceptance, as the case may be, the assigned Rating shall not be subject to surveillance and ICRA shall not be responsible for the continuous monitoring/surveillance of the assigned Rating.</span></li>
        </ol>
        <p class="c1 c4 c15"><span class="c2"></span></p>
        <ol class="c13 lst-kix_list_9-0" start="4">
            <li class="c1 c6 li-bullet-0"><span class="c2">You will only use each requested Rating for its intended purpose and will not use it for any other purpose.</span></li>
        </ol>
        <p class="c1 c27 c4 c83"><span class="c2"></span></p>
        <ol class="c13 lst-kix_list_7-0" start="5">
            <li class="c1 c6 li-bullet-0"><span class="c19 c5 c3">Tenure of the Agreement</span></li>
        </ol>
        <p class="c1 c4"><span class="c2"></span></p>
        <ol class="c13 lst-kix_list_5-0 start" start="1">
            <li class="c1 c6 li-bullet-0"><span class="c3">This Agreement shall remain valid till the earlier of the date that the Rating assigned is withdrawn or the date that there are no longer any amounts outstanding against the PTC. This Agreement cannot be terminated by your Company once it has accepted or used the Rating.</span></li>
        </ol>
        <p class="c1 c4 c15"><span class="c2"></span></p>
        <ol class="c13 lst-kix_list_5-0" start="2">
            <li class="c1 c6 li-bullet-0"><span class="c3">Notwithstanding clause E (I) above, the provisions of clauses K (Warranty), L (Confidentiality), M (Applicant Confidentiality for Unpublished ratings), N (Indemnification), O (Limitation of Liability), P (Warranties with respect to information provided to ICRA), Q (Use of information) and T (IV) shall survive any termination of the Agreement.</span></li>
        </ol>
        <p class="c1 c4"><span class="c2"></span></p>
        <ol class="c13 lst-kix_list_7-0" start="6">
            <li class="c1 c6 li-bullet-0"><span class="c19 c5 c3">Changes in Rating</span></li>
        </ol>
        <p class="c1 c4"><span class="c19 c5 c3"></span></p>
        <ol class="c13 lst-kix_list_4-0 start" start="1">
            <li class="c1 c6 li-bullet-0"><span class="c2">Subject to the terms and conditions of this Agreement, ICRA will keep the accepted Rating under surveillance until the earlier of the date that the Rating is withdrawn, in accordance with the provisions of the Regulations or the date that there are no longer any amounts outstanding against the PTCs. Following surveillance, ICRA may reaffirm, upgrade, downgrade, or withdraw the Rating (to the extent permitted by the Regulations); further, it may assign an outlook, or change or withdraw the outlook previously assigned; it may also place the Rating (previously assigned) on rating watch (with or without specified implications) or remove it from rating watch.  </span></li>
        </ol>
        <p class="c1 c4 c15"><span class="c78 c73 c5 c3 c42"></span></p>
        <ol class="c13 lst-kix_list_4-0" start="2">
            <li class="c1 c32 c15 li-bullet-1"><span class="c2">At any stage, failure on your part to furnish such information as ICRA may require from time to time, or failure to properly answer queries in a timely manner that may be raised by ICRA or failure on your part to pay Surveillance Fee, will result in ICRA carrying out the Rating surveillance on the basis of best available information. In addition, to the extent permitted by the Regulations, such failure on your part could result in ICRA withdrawing or revising the Rating assigned and disclose the rating outcome (inclusive of any reiterated/updated or modified Rating) as a non-cooperation Rating as required under the Regulations and not under contractual obligations under this Agreement. Notwithstanding the foregoing, the provisions of Clauses C, E, F, I, J, K, L, M, N, O, P, Q, S and T hereof shall, continue to apply to the Company and the Rating  in accordance with the terms hereof.</span></li>
        </ol>
        <p class="c1 c4 c15"><span class="c2"></span></p>
        <ol class="c13 lst-kix_list_4-0" start="3">
            <li class="c1 c6 li-bullet-0"><span class="c2">At any point, if ICRA is of the opinion that the circumstances then prevailing justify change, or withdrawal of the Rating, to the extent permitted by the Regulations, or warrant that the Rating be maintained at the existing level, it shall have the right to take the appropriate rating action, and such a decision shall be final and binding on your Company.</span></li>
        </ol>
        <p class="c1 c4 c15"><span class="c2"></span></p>
        <p class="c1 c4"><span class="c2"></span></p>
        <ol class="c13 lst-kix_list_7-0" start="7">
            <li class="c1 c6 li-bullet-0"><span class="c5 c3">Dissemination of Rating</span></li>
        </ol>
        <p class="c1 c4 c15"><span class="c2"></span></p>
        <ol class="c13 lst-kix_list_8-0 start" start="1">
            <li class="c1 c6 li-bullet-0"><span class="c2">ICRA shall communicate its rating decision in terms of assignment or change (inclusive of any suspension or withdrawal, to the extent permitted by the Regulations) in the Rating to you in writing, and contemporaneously therewith, such initial Rating or change (in each case, inclusive of the rationale therefor, outlook and such other relevant information) shall be published in a press release in accordance with the Regulations. ICRA shall disclose both the ratings i.e. unsupported ratings without factoring in the explicit credit enhancement and supported rating after factoring in the explicit credit enhancement, as applicable, in the press release. In case either of the ratings is not accepted, both ratings shall be considered as unaccepted by the Company.</span></li>
        </ol>
        <p class="c1 c4 c15"><span class="c2"></span></p>
        <ol class="c13 lst-kix_list_8-0" start="2">
            <li class="c1 c54 li-bullet-4"><span class="c2">In case of non-cooperation on your part for the surveillance, the published Rating (or any change thereof, as appropriate) and the Rating symbol will be accompanied with a disclaimer stating that due to your non-co-operation, the Rating is based on best available information. </span></li>
        </ol>
        <p class="c1 c15"><span class="c2">&nbsp;</span></p>
        <ol class="c13 lst-kix_list_8-0" start="3">
            <li class="c1 c54 li-bullet-4"><span class="c2">ICRA reserves the right to publish an unaccepted Rating, as set out in clause D (I), along with the details required under the Regulations.</span></li>
        </ol>
